description_en:
A polar text adventure game that pays tribute to "Lifeline". You are the first mate of the polar research ship Captain - the ship hit ice and sank in a snowstorm. You drifted to the ruins on the shore, with only a torn mainsail left in your hand. The game contains 26 different endings and the average game time is 20-30 minutes. 26 unique endings: three types (success/failure/mysterious) Ending illustration: 26 lights, one lit up after each achievement, replacing the traditional time ranking list; Resource management system: real-time changes in body temperature and satiety, narrative warning (no numbers displayed); Immersive interaction: triple interaction of physical buttons, shaking sensor, and sound effect feedback;
Exquisite Chinese typesetting: optimized for 1.14-inch 135x240 screen, 4 words x 5 lines of content per screen
Start-up melody: A minor "Sail Sail" motive; purely offline: no need to configure the network, you can start playing immediately.
